; The waves, for sprig(1).  Each line is one wave:
;
;	COUNT KIND SPEED SPREAD
;
; COUNT is how many come at once - and how many Dis processes the game
; starts, because in this one an entity IS a process.  KIND is flit or
; borer.  SPEED is hundredths of a pixel a frame downward.  SPREAD is
; how far a flit wanders sideways, in pixels, and is ignored by borers.
;
; Nothing here is in the program.  Making the last wave forty deep is
; editing this file, and procbench(1) says what forty processes cost.

%

 6 flit  55 40
 8 flit  70 34
 6 borer 95  0
10 flit  80 44
 8 borer 110 0
12 flit  95 50
14 borer 120 0
16 flit 105 56
